-- Table and column descriptions. Applied on every start (COMMENT ON is idempotent), so existing data keeps them too.
-- ---------- descriptions (shown on the Data page; read with obj_description / col_description) ----------
COMMENT ON TABLE applications IS 'Application service. A desktop app sold on the marketplace, made by a vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN applications.code IS 'Readable unique code for seeds and URLs; the key is id.';
COMMENT ON TABLE plans IS 'Catalog. A way to license one app (slots, licensing model). Sold only through offering items.';
COMMENT ON TABLE credit_packages IS 'Catalog. A number of credits and how many days a lot of them lives.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_packages.application_id IS 'Set for an in-app pack: the lot is scoped to this one app (sold inside the app). NULL: platform pack, usable in every app, or the apps of the offering it ships in.';
COMMENT ON TABLE offerings IS 'Catalog. A sellable product: one price for one or more items (plans and credit packages). single = one app, bundle = several apps (+ credits), credit_pack = credits only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN offerings.price_minor IS 'Price in minor units (cents) of currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN offerings.billing_period IS 'month = recurring subscription, one_time = single purchase (credit pack).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN offerings.trial_days IS 'Trial of the whole offering (moved here from plans: a bundle has one trial, not one per app).';
COMMENT ON TABLE offering_items IS 'Catalog. One position of an offering: exactly one of plan_id or credit_package_id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN offering_items.allocation_weight IS 'Share of the offering price for this item (minor units). Splits revenue between vendors and drives the partial refund (apps by unused time, credits by unspent share).';
COMMENT ON TABLE action_prices IS 'Catalog. Price in credits of one AI action in one app, versioned by valid_from. The client price; provider token cost is separate.';
COMMENT ON TABLE customers IS 'Customer service. The person who buys. handle is a readable unique name; the key is id.';
COMMENT ON TABLE subscriptions IS 'Billing (Billing team, simulated). One purchase of an offering by a customer; one_time purchases are a single-period subscription. Status moves only by allowed transitions; canceled is terminal.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN subscriptions.provider_sub_ref IS 'Subscription id at the payment provider; webhooks are matched by it.';
COMMENT ON TABLE payments IS 'Billing (simulated). One paid period. Each payment grants rights once: licenses per plan item, a lot per credit item.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN payments.payment_ref IS 'Payment id at the provider. Unique: a duplicate invoice.paid finds it and grants nothing.';
COMMENT ON TABLE licenses IS 'License service. Right to use an app: UNIQUE (subscription_id, offering_item_id): one license per app per subscription, a replayed event cannot add a second. Active until due_date. A bundle gives N licenses; an app may have licenses from several subscriptions.';
COMMENT ON TABLE credit_accounts IS 'Credits. The wallet: one per customer. Locked FOR UPDATE first in every charge (serializes a customer''s charges, avoids deadlock).';
COMMENT ON TABLE credit_lots IS 'Credits. A batch of credits from one payment item: where it may be spent (scope), what kind (paid/bonus), how much is left, when it expires. UNIQUE (payment_id, offering_item_id): Billing may deliver PaymentSucceeded twice; the second insert hits this key and grants nothing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.scope IS 'platform = any app; bundle = only the apps in lot_scope_apps (credits that came with apps).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.remaining IS 'Credits left. Always equals the sum of this lot''s ledger deltas; never negative (CHECK).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.revoked_at IS 'When the payment that granted this lot was refunded. Set on every lot of the payment, even one at 0, so credits a still-running charge returns later are burned again.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.expires_at IS 'End of the paid period (subscription credits) or purchase + validity (pack). Unspent credits are a liability until spent or expired.';
COMMENT ON TABLE lot_scope_apps IS 'Credits. Apps where a scope=bundle lot may be spent.';
COMMENT ON TABLE credit_charges IS 'Credits. One AI action charged to a wallet. Unique (account_id, idempotency_key): a retry replays the stored result instead of charging again. A 402 is not stored.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_charges.request_hash IS 'Hash of app + action + input: the same key with another body is refused with 422.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_charges.amount IS 'Price of the action from action_prices valid at charge time, copied here: a later price change never touches past charges.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_charges.result IS 'AI result kept for replays of the same idempotency key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_charges.cost_minor IS 'What the AI provider cost us (internal), for margin reports. In the MVP a stub: half the price in credits.';
COMMENT ON TABLE credit_ledger IS 'Credits. Append-only journal of every credit movement: grant, charge, refund, expire, revoke. Never updated or deleted; balances are derived from it.';
COMMENT ON TABLE webhook_events IS 'Billing (simulated). Inbox of provider webhooks: dedup by event_id; status applied / duplicate / parked (unknown subscription, retried later) / rejected.';
COMMENT ON TABLE provider_txns IS 'Mock payment provider''s own records: the other side of daily reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON TABLE sim_clock IS 'Simulator. Offset added to real time so "+31 days" moves renewals and expiry.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.source_type IS 'Where the lot came from: bundle (credits that came with a bundle), subscription (monthly credits of a single-app subscription), pack (bought credits) or promo (granted free). Shown to the customer as the source.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.payment_id IS 'Payment that granted this lot. A refund of that payment revokes exactly the lots it granted, not lots of other periods.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.offering_item_id IS 'Offering item (credit package) the lot comes from; with payment_id it is unique, so a replayed event cannot grant twice.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.subscription_id IS 'Subscription the lot belongs to: lots of one subscription are shown and cancelled together.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.label IS 'What the customer sees in the balance breakdown, e.g. "Design+ bundle · Oct 26".';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_lots.kind IS 'paid or bonus. Bonus credits go first and are never refunded as money.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_ledger.type IS 'grant, charge, refund (our-side failure), expire (unspent credits become revenue), revoke (payment refunded).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_ledger.delta IS 'Signed change of the lot. The sum of deltas of a lot always equals its remaining.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN credit_ledger.note IS 'Why: the action code for a charge, the failure for a refund.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN payments.refunded_minor IS 'Amount returned to the customer for this payment, minor units.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN payments.period_start IS 'Start of the period this payment pays for; renewals add one payment per period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN payments.status IS 'succeeded: paid, rights granted. refunded: money returned (full or partial, see refunded_minor); lots of this payment revoked. charged_back: the bank reversed it (design: revoke lots, block the credit account if credits were spent, manual review; not simulated in the MVP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN subscriptions.kind IS 'recurring (renews every period) or one_time (a credit pack: one payment, never renews).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN licenses.application_id IS 'Copied from offering_item → plan → application when the license is granted, in the same transaction. Deliberate denormalization: the hot check "does customer X have app Y" is answered by License alone, without joining Catalog tables across the service boundary. Safe because a plan never changes its application.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN licenses.customer_id IS 'Copied from the subscription at grant time, for the same access check by (customer_id, application_id).';
